course: dictionary
lesson: 9061
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Slide has many meanings, so the words around it are your clues. In «Add soap and the grease slides away», the grease moves smoothly off the surface, so slide is a verb about moving. Ask yourself: is something moving, or is it a thing you can touch?
explain: Slide can also be a noun, a thing. The playground slide is a structure you climb up and slide down. In a presentation, each slide is one page on the screen. «Standards slid» means they went slowly into a worse state, so nothing moved along a surface at all.
explain: Scientists use slide too. Friction slows things that slide, and smooth surfaces let things slide farther. «At the vet's, a microchip about the size of a grain of rice slides under the skin» shows something moving smoothly into place.
fact: Slide can be a verb (to slide, slides, slid, sliding) or a noun (a slide, slides).
fact: «Slide» means to move smoothly over a surface while staying in contact with it.
fact: A landslide is a fall of earth or rock.
fact: A microscope slide is a small glass piece for looking at things under a microscope.
fact: Friction slows things that slide; smooth surfaces let things slide farther.
exercise: «Add soap and the grease slides away.» What does slides mean here? | *To move smoothly over a surface and off it | To climb up a ladder | To shout loudly | To freeze solid
exercise: In the park, Maya climbs the steps and comes down the slide. What is the slide? | *A playground structure you climb up and slide down | A page on a screen | A small glass piece for a microscope | A fall of earth or rock
exercise: Find and copy one word from this list that means a fall of earth or rock. | *landslide | slid | sliding | smooth
test: «Standards slid.» What does slid mean here? | They were wrapped in paper | They were shiny and smooth | *They went slowly into a worse state | They went up very high
test: Why does playground safety say to go down the slide feet first, one at a time? | *To keep safe and avoid bumping into other children | To see who can slide the farthest | To make the slide go faster | Because climbing up is the rule
exam: In «The Earth turns 360 degrees in 24 hours, so noon slides westwards around the planet like a spotlight», what is slides doing? | Going into a worse state | *Moving smoothly and steadily around the planet | Being washed away with soap | Falling steeply, like a landslide
